diagram='''<figure aria-labelledby="system-caption"><svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 780 460" role="img" aria-labelledby="diagram-title diagram-desc"><title id="diagram-title">DUAT working set, archive and recovery architecture</title><desc id="diagram-desc">Linux keeps active source and tools. The project vault verifies candidates through restic and accesses the iPad archive via ifuse, an SSH USB bridge, and the Mac cable. Recovery returns archived files to new local storage. Receipts are retained on both endpoints.</desc><defs><marker id="arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8Z" fill="#916029"/></marker></defs><rect x="1" y="1" width="778" height="458" fill="#f5f8fa" stroke="#cedae2"/><rect x="25" y="30" width="300" height="115" rx="5" fill="#173e59"/><text x="45" y="61" class="label light">Linux • active working set</text><text x="45" y="88" class="small light">Source, compiler pins, live builds</text><text x="45" y="112" class="small light">Unique evidence stays available locally</text><rect x="455" y="30" width="300" height="115" rx="5" fill="#173e59"/><text x="475" y="61" class="label light">iPad • retained archive</text><text x="475" y="88" class="small light">Documents / TryOmarchy / Repository</text><text x="475" y="112" class="small light">Versioned snapshots + recovery records</text><path d="M325 63 H449" fill="none" stroke="#916029" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/><text x="350" y="51" class="tiny">SAVE</text><path d="M455 124 H331" fill="none" stroke="#916029" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/><text x="349" y="112" class="tiny">RECOVER</text><rect x="25" y="190" width="730" height="78" rx="5" fill="#e5eef4" stroke="#cedae2"/><text x="45" y="220" class="label">The connection path</text><text x="45" y="245" class="small">restic → ifuse → SSH Unix socket → Mac usbmuxd → USB → iPad app</text><path d="M175 145 V184 M605 145 V184" stroke="#916029" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/><rect x="25" y="300" width="730" height="127" rx="5" fill="white" stroke="#cedae2"/><text x="45" y="331" class="label">The retirement gate</text><text x="45" y="359" class="small">Full candidate restore → SHA-256 + metadata comparison → receipt readback</text><text x="45" y="383" class="small">Recheck activity and pins → quarantine → compare → retire local original</text><text x="45" y="409" class="tiny">Offloaded data has one physical archive device. Whole-scope recovery remains a separate test.</text></svg><figcaption id="system-caption">Architecture overview. The arrows describe file movement and recovery, not measured bandwidth. Automatic backups and explicit local retirement are separate workflows.</figcaption></figure>'''
cover='''<header class="cover"><div class="cover-inner"><div class="eyebrow">DUAT Vault / storage architecture</div><h1>DUAT Vault</h1><div class="subtitle">Verified Project Storage<br>and Recovery</div><p>A technical white paper on the iPad-backed archive, the Linux working set, and the recovery checks that connect them.</p><div class="seal"><svg width="36" height="36" viewBox="0 0 36 36" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 2 33 10v16L18 34 3 26V10Z M3 10l15 9 15-9M18 19v15" fill="none" stroke="#d7bd94" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg><span>ARCHITECTURE &amp; OPERATOR HANDBOOK<br>Public architecture edition · Implementation: project-vault / restic</span></div></div></header>'''
